\cf2 The method's main weakness: we might mistake textual silence for falsification. Just because Ezekiel 4-5 doesn't show God accepting intercession doesn't mean he never does - it means he doesn't here, under these conditions.\
Its strength: when something is explicitly contradicted, we have solid ground. If people assume divine judgment is arbitrary or emotional, the precise weighing and measuring falsifies this definitively.\
